Stop pinning new tab groups to the bookmarks bar, and drop the toggle for it.

Chromium registers kAutoPinNewTabGroups as true, so every tab group anyone
creates - on this machine or, through sync, on any other - is pinned to the
bookmarks bar without being asked. The bookmarks bar is a place people arrange
themselves; a browser writing to it on its own initiative is the kind of thing
that gets noticed only after it has happened a few times.

Two changes, and the second is the reason for the first.

The default goes to false. That alone would be enough to stop the behaviour,
but it would leave a switch in Settings whose only job is to turn something
back on that nobody asked for.

So the switch goes too. "Automatically pin new tab groups created on any
device to the bookmarks bar" is removed from Settings > Appearance. It sits
between "Show tab groups in bookmarks bar" and the Ctrl-Tab MRU toggle, both
of which stay - they describe how existing things are displayed rather than
authorising the browser to create bookmarks.

Nothing in appearance_page.ts refers to the element, so removing it from the
template is the whole change on that side. IDS_SETTINGS_AUTO_PIN_NEW_TAB_GROUPS
stays registered and simply goes unused, which costs a string in the .pak and
avoids touching settings_localized_strings_provider.cc, which several other
patches in this series already edit.

The pref stays SYNCABLE_PREF. Aerium ships no sync, so it never travels, and
leaving the registration shape alone keeps the diff to the one value that
matters.

--- a/components/saved_tab_groups/public/pref_names.cc
+++ b/components/saved_tab_groups/public/pref_names.cc
@@ -32,8 +32,12 @@
       prefs::kStopShowingTabGroupConfirmationOnTabClose, false);
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
 
+  // Aerium: off by default. Upstream pins every new tab group to the bookmarks
+  // bar without being asked, and the settings toggle that undid it is removed
+  // too - a browser should not rearrange someone's bookmarks bar on its own,
+  // and an option to stop it doing that is not the same as not doing it.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      kAutoPinNewTabGroups, true,
+      kAutoPinNewTabGroups, false,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
 
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kSavedTabGroupSpecificsToDataMigration,
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/appearance_page.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/appearance_page.html
@@ -245,12 +245,6 @@
             hidden="[[showProjectsPanelEnabled_]]">
         </settings-toggle-button>
 
-        <settings-toggle-button class="hr" id="autoPinNewTabGroups"
-            pref="{{prefs.auto_pin_new_tab_groups}}"
-            label="$i18n{autoPinNewTabGroups}"
-            hidden="[[showProjectsPanelEnabled_]]">
-        </settings-toggle-button>
-
         <template is="dom-if" if="[[showCtrlTabMru_]]">
           <settings-toggle-button class="hr" id="ctrlTabMru"
               pref="{{prefs.browser.ctrl_tab_mru}}"
